From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32: GetProcAddress is its own export (6544)

kernel32 forwarded GetProcAddress to kernelbase ("kernelbase.GetProcAddress"
in its export table). Windows' kernel32 exports it as code, as it does
LoadLibrary* and GetModuleHandle*, which Wine already exports as import
thunks. PotPlayer's packer reads kernel32's export table to find
GetProcAddress and cannot follow a forwarder without it: it called a null
pointer, its handler returned an invalid disposition and the main thread
overflowed its stack before any window. GetProcAddress is now an import
thunk too (-import: a jump to kernelbase's, so Delphi's register
assumptions there still hold).
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
--- a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
@@ -796,7 +796,7 @@
 @ stdcall GetPrivateProfileStringW(wstr wstr wstr ptr long wstr)
 @ stdcall GetPrivateProfileStructA (str str ptr long str)
 @ stdcall GetPrivateProfileStructW(wstr wstr ptr long wstr)
-@ stdcall GetProcAddress(long str) kernelbase.GetProcAddress
+@ stdcall -import GetProcAddress(long str)
 @ stdcall GetProcessAffinityMask(long ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall GetProcessDEPPolicy(long ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall -import GetProcessDefaultCpuSets(ptr ptr long ptr)
